{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"MA security deposit liability on transfer of the dwelling unit","requirement":"A lessor who transfers the dwelling unit remains liable under § 15B until the deposit is credited to the successor and the tenant is notified; if the lessor fails to credit it, the successor assumes liability for the deposit and accrued interest.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who receive a security deposit or rental advance and transfer their interest in the dwelling unit, and their successors in interest.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Lessors transferring interest in a dwelling unit and their successors"},"exemptions":"Liability does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter sixty, a foreclosing mortgagee, or a mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"Upon such transfer, the lessor or his agent shall continue to be liable with respect to the provisions of this section until:--(a) there has been a credit of the amount of the rental advance so held to the lessor's successor in interest and the tenant has been notified in writing of the transfer and of the successor in interest's name, business address, and business telephone number;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"MA § 15B anti-waiver and conflicting lease provisions void","requirement":"Any lease provision that conflicts with § 15B, and any waiver of its provisions by a tenant or prospective tenant, is against public policy and void and unenforceable.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to all leases and tenancies governed by § 15B and to tenants and prospective tenants.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Conflicting lease provisions and tenant waivers are deemed void and unenforceable.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(8) Any provision of a lease which conflicts with any provision of this section and any waiver by a tenant or prospective tenant of any provision of this section shall be deemed to be against public policy and therefore void and unenforceable.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-02","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"MA § 15B exemption for short-term vacation rentals","requirement":"Section 15B does not apply to a lease, rental, occupancy or tenancy of 100 days or less that is for a vacation or recreational purpose.","key_value":"100 days or less","coverage_conditions":"Applies to leases and tenancies governed by § 15B generally; short-term vacation and recreational rentals of 100 days or less are excluded.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Leases of 100 days or less for vacation or recreational purposes"},"exemptions":"Leases, rentals, occupancies or tenancies of 100 days or less in duration for a vacation or recreational purpose.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(9) The provisions of this section shall not apply to any lease, rental, occupancy or tenancy of one hundred days or less in duration which lease or rental is for a vacation or recreational purpose.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
